  "ai_show_review": {
    "summary": "High‑energy Lakeland ’82 show with monster Not Fade Away & tight second set",
    "review": "The September 12, 1982 gig at the Lakeland Civic Center captures the band in a high‑octane groove that still feels fresh. The first set rolls solidly through classics like \"Alabama Getaway\" and \"Might As Well,\" but it’s the second set where the magic erupts – a fire‑breathing \"Playing In The Band\" rockets into an inspired drum duet, space, and then lands on a soaring \"The Wheel\" that segues straight into a monster \"Not Fade Away.\" Brent Mydland’s B‑3 organ shines on that closer, while Mickey Hart and Bill Kreutzmann trade jazzy, responsive fills. Jerry’s guitar work is on fire (especially his solo on \"Might As Well\") even if his vocals show a hint of fatigue, and Phil’s bass, though occasionally buried in the mix, still provides the steady anchor for the improvisations. Overall the band sounds locked‑in, delivering one of the more memorable 1982 performances.",
